Pending fix for C5 (code review of 2026-11-09). Native blank() treats only ASCII whitespace as blank,
so native compare and finalize accept a rationale, quote or reviewer made only of Unicode spaces
(NBSP, U+3000, U+2028, U+FEFF and others), which every JavaScript validator rejects with trim().
This patch makes the blank() in src/grader.cpp reuse the ECMAScript trim() in src/certificate.cpp
and adds native-core cases.

Both files are pinned by edge/build-info.json to the committed WebAssembly module, so apply the
patch only together with a rebuild of that module:
  1. git apply patches/c5-native-blank-unicode.patch, git rm this file, and commit.
  2. From that commit, rebuild with emsdk 6.0.13 (EMSDK=/path/to/emsdk npm run build:edge, or the
     build-edge.yml workflow).
  3. node wasm/check.mjs
  4. Write that commit's SHA to edge/source-commit.txt.
  5. Commit edge/avenquellis-grader-runtime.js and .wasm, edge/build-info.json and
     edge/source-commit.txt.
  6. npm test, and ctest in a CMake build tree.
patches/s2.4-native-reviewer-utf16-units.patch waits for the same rebuild. The two patches are
independent and apply in either order: apply both in step 1 and rebuild once.
Checked on a copy of the fix branch: a -Werror Release build with no warnings and CTest 5/5; the
new native-core cases fail without the grader change; in JavaScript only the manifest hash test
fails, as expected until the rebuild.

